The direct values are independent 110-decimal eigenvalues of T^T T.  The
closed values use the finite sums in the derivation, while ``pencil`` is a
separate numerical solution of the four-state generalized eigenproblem.
``eps_over_phi2`` is the exact inverse-tail Frobenius bound divided by the
smaller nonzero singular value of the rank-two comparison matrix; it is an
upper bound, not the observed relative error.
